# <PROJECT NAME> — always-on instructions

**This file is a pointer, not a rule book.**

It is loaded **in full, at the start of every session, however long it is** — length is not
truncated, it is simply charged. That has two consequences that decide its whole shape:

1. **Everything here is charged to every task**, including the ones it has nothing to do with, and
   longer files are documented to reduce adherence. Target under 200 lines.
2. **Nothing here is gated.** If it lives outside the repository it describes, no CI can read it,
   nothing can diff it against the system it documents, and a rule kept here drifts silently.

So the substance lives where it can be checked, and this file says only where that is.

<!--
